# TEC Design Docs

Design and UX reference material for the TEC API proof of concept: grey-box blockframes and a nested-navigation demo for the GOV.UK Tech Docs sidebar.

Technical architecture documentation lives on a separate Tech Docs site: [http://localhost:4568](http://localhost:4568).

## Contents

- [Penalty charge numbers](/penalty-charge-numbers.html) — PCN stem and suffix, and how the check digit is calculated
- [TEC PCN blockframes](/tec-pcn-blockframes.html) — grey-box wireframes for case tabs and Next steps journeys
- [ExUI form elements](/exui-form-elements.html) — isolated CCD / ExUI field-type controls
- [Caseworker journeys](/caseworker-journeys.html) — enter a general application from Case details, plus validation-failure and exception review
- [Case officer journeys](/case-officer-journeys.html) — review an out-of-time refusal decision
- [Local authority journeys](/local-authority-journeys.html) — upload a batch file, and review an out-of-time application
- [Local demo cases](/local-demo-cases.html) — seeded Manage Cases examples (regenerate links locally)
- [Email notifications](/email-notifications.html) — larger-scale blockframes for LA and respondent emails
- [Nesting demonstration](/nesting-demo/) — example multi-level sidebar from nested folders

## Run locally

Start the application and documentation sites together:

```bash
./gradlew bootWithCCD
```

Design docs preview: [http://localhost:4567](http://localhost:4567). Tech docs: [http://localhost:4568](http://localhost:4568). See the repository README for the full local service list and clerk login.
